{
  "message": "The good news is that the design itself checks out. The emulation found no failures, and the whole flow is connected: sign-in, permission-checked keyword search, Gemini and cited answers. It's blocked because no generated code exists yet for these Google Cloud parts. The only typed Google Cloud contract we support is private object storage, and switching to it would shrink the scope, so we won't do that. The fix is product engineering work: native modules for Identity Platform, the Cloud Run web app and API, the Firestore catalog and the Vertex AI Gemini step. This exact project (revision 2, artifact 74f7326f…) can serve as the reproducer. Until those modules exist, nothing has tested real Gemini answers, Google Cloud permissions or a deployment. While that work is pending, let's settle the decision that's still open: which country must the synthetic documents and model processing stay in?",
